{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ושוב", :translit "v'shuv", :gloss "and returned"} {:he "ויצא יצוא ושוב עד יבושת המים", :translit "v'yatza y'tza v'shuv ad y'vushat ha-mayim", :gloss "and went out gone out and returned until the drying up of the waters"} {:he "והחיות רצוא ושוב", :translit "v'ha-chayot r'tzo v'shov", :gloss "and the living creatures ran and returned"} {:he "שמזיעת החיות יוצא נהר דינור", :translit "she-miziyat ha-chayot yotza nahar dinur", :gloss "from the sweat of the living creatures emerges the river of fire"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["ושוב" "ויצא יצוא ושוב" "והחיות רצוא ושוב"]}], :frame {:text "Rabbi Elazar stated that the river of fire (נהר דינור) emerges from the sweat of the living creatures (חיות) in the divine chariot, as recorded in Hagigah 13a. The word ושוב appears in Genesis 8:3 describing the return of flood waters, in Ezekiel 47:5 describing river water measurements, and in Ezekiel 1:14 describing the running and returning of the divine living creatures. Ba'al HaTurim links the Ezekiel 1:14 usage to the river of fire tradition from Hagigah 13a, then argues that since the word ושוב in Genesis 8:3 also concerns a river, it too partakes of the river of fire imagery.", :sources ["Hagigah 13a" "Ezekiel 47:5" "Ezekiel 1:14" "Genesis 8:3"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["ושוב" "ויצא יצוא ושוב" "והחיות רצוא ושוב"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ושוב", :refs ["Genesis 8:3" "Genesis 8:7" "Genesis 31:13" "Joshua 5:2" "1 Samuel 15:25" "1 Samuel 15:30" "Jeremiah 3:1" "Ezekiel 1:14"], :n 9, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ויצא יצוא ושוב", :refs ["Genesis 8:7"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "והחיות רצוא ושוב", :refs ["Ezekiel 1:14"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:04:56.344403818Z", :model "glm-5.2"}